  "days_covered": 1,
  "state": "new",
  "last_novel": "2026-10-04",
  "primer": {
    "text": "Sudan's civil war is fought between SAF and RSF, rival armed forces each seeking control on the ground. The conflict has produced a humanitarian front centered on areas like Kordofan, where civilian sites such as a university dormitory, contested towns like al-Mazroub, and aid routes used by WFP trucks are at risk. That front is why outside leverage matters. The United States can use visas needed to attend the UN General Assembly (UNGA) as pressure to push the warring parties toward a ceasefire. In this context, UNGA is the United Nations General Assembly, the gathering of countries at the United Nations, and WFP is the humanitarian group that moves food aid.",
    "built_at": "2026-10-05T02:19:08.047608+00:00"
  },
  "current": {
    "date": "2026-10-04",
    "bottom_line": "Kordofan was the focal point Oct 1-4: a confirmed RSF drone strike on a university dormitory in El Obeid killed civilians, a reported WFP truck strike killed an aid driver in South Kordofan, and the army claimed a town recapture nearby. A UK statement at the UN on Oct 2 publicly blamed external weapons flows for sustaining the war. Confidence is high for the initial dormitory toll and the UK statement; the higher death toll, the town recapture, and the WFP strike rest on single unverified reports.",
    "escalation": {
      "direction": "steady",
      "pace": "gradual"
    },
    "coverage": "rising coverage",
    "source": "daily",
